 3.  Arduino Software (Arduino IDE) 
    arduino ide
    The Arduino IDE is used to write and upload code to Arduino boards.


How to Install:

1. Go to arduino.cc/en/software

2. Download the installer for your OS.

3. Run the installer and accept the default settings.

* Video Tutorial: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NxH5RNbIxBk


Finding the HEX File (for Simulation):

1. Open Arduino IDE -> File -> Preferences.

2. Check the box "Show verbose output during: compilation".

3. Compile your code. The bottom console will print the path to your .hex file.

* Video Tutorial: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oXjWl8tbyiA


